The second assert statement checks if the new list contains x is the same as the old list. 

The third assert statement checks if the new index of x is greater than or equal to the old index of x. 

The fourth assert statement checks if the new index of x is equal to the new count of the list minus 1 and if the new index of x is equal to the old index of x. 

The fifth assert statement checks if the new index of x is equal to the old index of x and if the new count of the list is equal to the old count of the list minus 1. 

